{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1467208","title":"A sustainable biohybrid strategy: Maintaining efficient nitrogen removal over long-term operation via EPS-induced biocompatibility in nZVI-amended sludge","description":"This study aims to evaluate the long-term operational stability and mechanistic adaptation of an EPS@nZVI-amended sludge system for advanced nitrogen removal. We hypothesize that the EPS-derived interface provides sustainable biocompatibility by guiding the transformation of nZVI into an electroactive mineral network while simultaneously shielding the microbial consortium from chronic oxidative stress. Through long-term reactor monitoring, multi-spectroscopic analysis of interface aging, and meta-omics including metagenome and metabolome, this work explores the transition from a \"toxicity-dominated\" initial stage to a \"synergy-dominated\" stable stage. This work seeks to provide a sustainable framework for the application of biohybrid nanomaterials in continuous wastewater purification.","center":"Tongji University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/05/17 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN60210716","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from activated sludge metagenome","uncertain",null,"2025-12-20",2025,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null,"activated sludge",null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN60210717","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from activated sludge metagenome","uncertain",null,"2025-12-20",2025,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null,"activated sludge",null,null,"environmental sample; urban association not established"],["SAMN60210718","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from activated sludge meta